                <td bgcolor="#f0f0f0" width="20%" valign="top"><b>Acceptance Criteria:</b></td>
                <td id="customfield_10032-209000-value" class="value" bgcolor="#ffffff" width="80%">      <h2><a name="AC1%3AInitiateBothEmailandEDICommunication"></a><ins>AC-1: Initiate Both Email and EDI Communication</ins></h2>

<p><b>Given</b> a valid standardized tender message is received<br/>
<b>And</b> the communication method is Email and EDI<br/>
<b>When</b> the Tender Dispatcher processes the message<br/>
<b>Then</b> it shall initiate an EDI tender submission<br/>
<b>And</b> it shall initiate an email tender communication<br/>
<b>And</b> both communications shall represent the same shipment, shipping option, carrier, and tender transaction.</p>

<h2><a name="AC2%3ASendtheEDITender"></a><ins>AC-2: Send the EDI Tender</ins></h2>

<p><b>Given</b> the communication method is Email and EDI<br/>
<b>When</b> the EDI communication is initiated<br/>
<b>Then</b> the standardized tender payload shall be submitted to the designated Boomi endpoint<br/>
<b>And</b> the EDI outcome shall be recorded independently.</p>

<h2><a name="AC3%3ASendtheEmailCopy"></a><ins>AC-3: Send the Email Copy</ins></h2>

<p><b>Given</b> the communication method is Email and EDI<br/>
<b>When</b> the email communication is initiated<br/>
<b>Then</b> a human-readable tender email shall be generated<br/>
<b>And</b> it shall be submitted to the configured carrier recipients<br/>
<b>And</b> the email outcome shall be recorded independently.</p>

<h2><a name="AC4%3AExcludeAcceptandDeclineActions"></a><ins>AC-4: Exclude Accept and Decline Actions</ins></h2>

<p><b>Given</b> an email is generated for the Email and EDI communication method<br/>
<b>When</b> the Email Communication Service builds the email<br/>
<b>Then</b> the review page of Email shall not contain Accept or Decline buttons or links<br/>
<b>And</b> it shall be used only as an informational tender copy.</p>

<h2><a name="AC5%3ABothCommunicationsSucceed"></a><ins>AC-5: Both Communications Succeed</ins></h2>

<p><b>Given</b> the Email and EDI communication method is being processed<br/>
<b>When</b> the mail server accepts the email request<br/>
<b>And</b> the designated Boomi endpoint accepts the EDI request<br/>
<b>Then</b> both channel outcomes shall be recorded as successful<br/>
<b>And</b> the combined communication shall be treated as successfully dispatched<br/>
<b>And</b> the tender shall move to the applicable successful status.</p>

<h2><a name="AC6%3ABothCommunicationsFail"></a><ins>AC-6: Both Communications Fail</ins></h2>

<p><b>Given</b> the Email and EDI communication method is being processed<br/>
<b>When</b> both the email and EDI submissions fail<br/>
<b>And</b> all applicable retries are exhausted<br/>
<b>Then</b> both channel failures shall be recorded<br/>
<b>And</b> the tender shall be updated to <b>Tender Failed</b><br/>
<b>And</b> the failure details shall be available for operational investigation.</p>

<h2><a name="AC7%3AEDISucceedsandEmailFails"></a><ins>AC-7: EDI Succeeds and Email Fails</ins></h2>

<p><b>Given</b> the Email and EDI communication method is being processed<br/>
<b>When</b> the designated Boomi endpoint accepts the EDI request<br/>
<b>And</b> the email submission fails<br/>
<b>Then</b> the EDI outcome shall be recorded as successful<br/>
<b>And</b> the email outcome shall be recorded as failed<br/>
<b>And</b> Tender should be considered as Tender Failed</p>


<h2><a name="AC8%3AEmailSucceedsandEDIFails"></a><ins>AC-8: Email Succeeds and EDI Fails</ins></h2>

<p><b>Given</b> the Email and EDI communication method is being processed<br/>
<b>When</b> the mail server accepts the email request<br/>
<b>And</b> the EDI submission fails<br/>
<b>Then</b> the email outcome shall be recorded as successful<br/>
<b>And</b> the EDI outcome shall be recorded as failed<br/>
<b>And</b> Tender should be considered as Tender Failed</p>

<h2><a name="AC9%3AOneChannelFailureDoesNotBlocktheOther"></a><ins>AC-9: One Channel Failure Does Not Block the Other</ins></h2>

<p><b>Given</b> the dispatcher encounters a failure while submitting the first communication<br/>
<b>When</b> the second communication has not yet been attempted<br/>
<b>Then</b> the dispatcher shall still attempt the second communication<br/>
<b>And</b> shall record the result of each channel separately.</p>

<h2><a name="AC10%3AReceiveaResponseThroughEDI"></a><ins>AC-10: Receive a Response Through EDI</ins></h2>

<p><b>Given</b> a tender was sent using Email and EDI<br/>
<b>When</b> a valid EDI response is received from the carrier<br/>
<b>Then</b> the response shall be processed through the standardized tender-response workflow<br/>
<b>And</b> it shall not be rejected because an email copy was also sent.</p>

<h2><a name="AC11%3AReceiveaResponseThroughAnotherSupportedChannel"></a><ins>AC-11: Receive a Response Through Another Supported Channel</ins></h2>

<p><b>Given</b> a tender was sent using Email and EDI<br/>
<b>When</b> the carrier submits a valid response through Net Native, manual update, API, or another supported channel<br/>
<b>Then</b> the response shall be processed according to the common tender-response rules<br/>
<b>And</b> it shall not be rejected solely because it was received through a different channel.</p>

<h2><a name="AC12%3AProcessaResponseAfterPartialCommunicationFailure"></a><ins>AC-12: Process a Response After Partial Communication Failure</ins></h2>

<p><b>Given</b> one outbound communication succeeded and the other failed<br/>
<b>When</b> a valid carrier response is received<br/>
<b>Then</b> the system shall process the response<br/>
<b>And</b> it shall not ignore or reject the response because one outbound channel failed.</p>
  </td>
            </tr>
