    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <h2><a name="BusinessSummary"></a><ins>Business Summary</ins></h2>

<p><b>As a</b> Tender Dispatcher,<br/>
<b>I want</b> to initiate both Email and EDI communication when the configured communication method is <b>Email and EDI</b>,<br/>
<b>So that</b> the carrier receives both a system-integrated EDI tender and a human-readable email copy.</p>

<h2><a name="BusinessContext"></a><ins>Business Context</ins></h2>

<p>Certain carriers require tender information through two communication channels:</p>

<ul>
	<li><b>EDI</b>, to load the tender into the carrier’s system automatically.</li>
	<li><b>Email</b>, to provide a human-readable copy to the carrier’s operational users.</li>
</ul>


<p>When the configured communication method is <b>Email and EDI</b>, the Tender Dispatcher shall initiate both communications using the same standardized tender request. The email serves as an informational copy and shall not provide Accept or Decline actions.  </p>

<p>The method used to send the tender shall not determine or restrict the method through which the carrier responds. A valid response may be received through EDI, Net Native, or another supported response channel and shall be processed independently of the original outbound communication method.</p>

<h1><a name="BusinessRules"></a><ins>Business Rules</ins></h1>

<h2><a name="BR1%3ACombinedCommunicationTrigger"></a>BR-1: Combined Communication Trigger</h2>

<p>The Tender Dispatcher shall initiate combined communication when the standardized tender message contains:</p>

<p><b>Communication Method = Email and EDI</b></p>

<p>The communication method shall be determined before the Tender Dispatcher receives the standardized tender request.</p>

<h2><a name="BR2%3ADualChannelDispatch"></a>BR-2: Dual-Channel Dispatch</h2>

<p>When the communication method is Email and EDI, the Tender Dispatcher shall initiate:</p>

<ol>
	<li>An EDI tender submission to the designated EDI integration service.</li>
	<li>An email tender copy to the designated Email Communication Service.</li>
</ol>


<p>Both requests shall originate from the same standardized tender message and represent the same shipment, shipping option, carrier, and tender transaction.</p>

<h2><a name="BR3%3AEDITenderProcessing"></a>BR-3: EDI Tender Processing</h2>

<p>The EDI tender shall be submitted to the designated Boomi endpoint in the agreed standardized format.</p>

<p>Boomi shall be responsible for:</p>

<ul>
	<li>transforming the tender payload into the required carrier-notification format;</li>
	<li>generating the applicable EDI transaction; and</li>
	<li>delivering the EDI tender through the existing carrier-integration process.</li>
</ul>


<p>From the Tender Dispatcher’s perspective, the EDI communication is successful when the designated Boomi endpoint successfully accepts the request.</p>

<h2><a name="BR4%3AEmailTenderCopy"></a>BR-4: Email Tender Copy</h2>

<p>The Email Communication Service shall generate and send a human-readable tender email to the configured carrier recipients.</p>

<p><del>The email may include:</del></p>

<ul>
	<li><del>shipment number;</del></li>
	<li><del>carrier information;</del></li>
	<li><del>origin and destination;</del></li>
	<li><del>pickup and delivery information;</del></li>
	<li><del>shipment details;</del></li>
	<li><del>special instructions;</del></li>
	<li><del>attachments or embedded tender content;</del></li>
	<li><del>other information required for carrier review.</del></li>
</ul>


<p>The final email template, content, and attachment requirements shall follow the approved business design.</p>

<h2><a name="BR5%3ANoAcceptorDeclineActionsintheEmail"></a>BR-5: No Accept or Decline Actions in the Email</h2>

<p>When the communication method is Email and EDI, the email shall not contain:</p>

<ul>
	<li>Email Body and Review Page both will be same as tender communication as email except one. In this scenario, Accept and Reject button will not be available in the Tender Review page.</li>
</ul>


<h2><a name="BR6%3AIndependentChannelProcessing"></a>BR-6: Independent Channel Processing</h2>

<p>The Email and EDI communication requests shall be processed independently.</p>

<p>A failure in one channel shall not prevent the Tender Dispatcher from attempting the other channel. For example:</p>

<ul>
	<li>If EDI submission fails, the system shall still attempt to send the email.</li>
	<li>If email submission fails, the system shall still attempt to send the EDI tender.</li>
</ul>


<p>This ensures that the carrier may still receive the tender through one of the configured channels.</p>

<h2><a name="BR7%3AChannelLevelOutcomeTracking"></a>BR-7: Channel-Level Outcome Tracking</h2>

<p>The system shall maintain the outcome of each communication attempt independently.</p>

<p>For the same tender transaction, the system shall capture:</p>

<ul>
	<li>EDI submission status;</li>
	<li>Email submission status;</li>
	<li>EDI submission timestamp;</li>
	<li>Email submission timestamp;</li>
	<li><del>number of attempts for each channel;</del></li>
	<li>failure reason for each unsuccessful channel; and</li>
	<li>correlation or transaction identifier.</li>
</ul>


<h2><a name="BR8%3ABothChannelsSuccessful"></a>BR-8: Both Channels Successful</h2>

<p>When both EDI and Email submissions succeed:</p>

<ul>
	<li>the combined communication shall be treated as successfully dispatched;</li>
	<li>the successful outcome of both channels shall be recorded; and</li>
	<li>the tender shall move to the applicable successful status, such as <b>Sent</b>.</li>
</ul>


<h2><a name="BR9%3ABothChannelsFailed"></a>BR-9: Both Channels Failed</h2>

<p>When both EDI and Email submissions fail:</p>

<ul>
	<li>the combined tender communication shall be treated as failed;</li>
	<li>each channel’s failure reason shall be captured;</li>
	<li>retry rules shall be applied independently to each channel; and</li>
	<li>the tender shall move to <b>Tender Failed</b> when applicable retries are exhausted.</li>
</ul>


<h2><a name="BR10%3APartialCommunicationFailureshouldbeconsideredasFailure"></a>BR-10: Partial Communication Failure should be considered as Failure</h2>

<p>A partial communication failure occurs when:</p>

<ul>
	<li>EDI succeeds and Email fails; or</li>
	<li>Email succeeds and EDI fails.</li>
</ul>


<p>The system shall record the individual outcome of each channel so that operations and support users can determine which communication succeeded and which failed.</p>

<p>But, overall tender communication will be considered as failure. So, tender status should be <b>Tender Failed</b> and shipment status should be <b>User Review</b>.</p>

<h2><a name="BR12%3AResponseMethodIndependence"></a>BR-12: Response Method Independence</h2>

<p>The original tender communication method shall not restrict the carrier’s response method.</p>

<p>A valid carrier response may be received through any supported method, including:</p>

<ul>
	<li>EDI Update;</li>
	<li>Net-Native Update;</li>
	<li>Manual Update;</li>
	<li>API Update</li>
	<li>Automatic Update</li>
	<li>Email Links Update</li>
</ul>


<p>The response shall be validated and processed based on its tender and shipment identifiers, not solely on the method used to send the tender.</p>

<h2><a name="BR13%3AProcessaResponseAfterPartialDelivery"></a>BR-13: Process a Response After Partial Delivery</h2>

<p>If one outbound channel succeeded and the other failed, a valid carrier response received through a supported channel shall still be processed.</p>

<p>The system shall not reject a valid response solely because:</p>

<ul>
	<li>one of the two outbound communication attempts failed; or</li>
	<li>the response arrived through a different method than the successful outbound channel.</li>
</ul>


<h2><a name="BR14%3ACommunicationSuccessBoundaries"></a>BR-14: Communication Success Boundaries</h2>

<p>For the combined communication:</p>

<ul>
	<li>Email is successful when the configured mail server accepts the email request.</li>
	<li>EDI is successful when the designated Boomi endpoint accepts the EDI tender request.</li>
</ul>


<p>A successful submission does not confirm that the carrier reviewed or accepted the tender.</p>
            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

